---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Humanoid Robot Stocks: Who Makes the Bots';
const desc = 'The verified humanoid robot makers and their supply chain: Tesla, UBTech, Unitree, and the compute layer. Built from the Robotics Supply-Chain Intelligence 2026 dataset, every ticker checked.';

const makers = [
  { name: 'Tesla', ticker: 'TSLA', exchange: 'NASDAQ', role: 'Optimus humanoid program inside a car company', layer: 'Curated core (verified)' },
  { name: 'UBTech', ticker: '9888.HK', exchange: 'HKEX', role: 'Listed Chinese humanoid OEM, mass-production shipments', layer: 'Curated core (verified)' },
  { name: 'Unitree', ticker: 'Post-IPO, Aug 19 2026', exchange: 'China A-share', role: 'Mass-produced humanoid that opened its IPO at +629%', layer: 'IPO documented in our timeline; see Unitree page' },
  { name: 'NVIDIA', ticker: 'NVDA', exchange: 'NASDAQ', role: 'Compute layer: the brains most humanoids run on', layer: 'Curated core (verified)' },
];

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: 'Verified humanoid robot makers and compute suppliers',
  description: 'Public companies building or supplying humanoid robots, from the curated Tier-A core of the Robotics Supply-Chain Intelligence 2026 dataset.',
  url: Astro.url.href,
  dateCreated: '2026-08-30',
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'vhsgreed', url: Astro.site?.toString() },
  distribution: { '@type': 'DataDownload', encodingFormat: 'CSV', contentUrl: 'https://store.vhsgreed.win/l/robotics-supply-chain-database-2026' },
  variableMeasured: `${makers.length} companies`,
  includedInDataCatalog: { '@type': 'DataCatalog', name: 'Robotics Supply-Chain Intelligence 2026' },
};
---
<Base title={title} description={desc}>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Humanoid robot stocks: who makes the bots</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The humanoids are real: they run, climb, and ship in the thousands. If
        you want equity exposure to the robots themselves, these are the
        verified makers and their compute supplier, with the verification layer
        stated for every row.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn-accent" href="https://store.vhsgreed.win/l/robotics-supply-chain-database-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track="gumroad_click">Get the full dataset</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/robotics-stocks/robotics-etf-vs-stocks/">ETFs vs direct stocks</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <section class="section-tight">
      <h2>Verified humanoid OEMs and the compute layer</h2>
      <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Company</th>
              <th>Ticker</th>
              <th>Exchange</th>
              <th>Humanoid role</th>
              <th>Verification layer</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {makers.map((c) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{c.name}</td>
                <td><span class="mono">{c.ticker}</span></td>
                <td>{c.exchange}</td>
                <td>{c.role}</td>
                <td><span class="muted">{c.layer}</span></td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="prose section-tight" style="max-width: 72ch;">
      <h2>The Unitree lesson: price discovery ran ahead of the listing</h2>
      <p>
        Unitree, the company behind the mass-produced humanoid, went public on
        August 19, 2026 at a $66B peak valuation and opened at +629%. Its
        pre-IPO crypto perps on Hyperliquid had priced it 75% below that open,
        turning over $59M with $9.1M open interest before any share traded. We
        documented the full case in <a href="/robotics-stocks/unitree-ipo/">Unitree IPO explained</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Where the bots actually come from</h2>
      <p>
        China is 63-70% of the robotics supply chain by our build, which means
        most humanoid production, and most of the component layer beneath it,
        sits in one jurisdiction. That is a concentration fact, not an opinion,
        and it shapes every access question: which listing you can buy, in
        which currency, through which broker.
      </p>

      <h2>Honest limits</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Identity and tickers are confirmed at harvest; business relevance is a heuristic filter in places.</li>
        <li>Index and quote verification is point-in-time (2026-08-30), not forever.</li>
        <li>Some humanoid programs sit inside private companies. We flag them private rather than guess a ticker; KUKA is the documented example.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Related pages</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/robotics-stocks/actuator-stocks/">Actuator stocks: the pick-and-shovel play</a></li>
        <li><a href="/robotics-stocks/unitree-ipo/">Unitree IPO explained: the +629% open</a></li>
        <li><a href="/robotics-stocks/">Robotics stocks by country</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/insights/robotics-supply-chain-2026/">The full writeup: mapping the robotics supply chain</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
</Base>
